# TaurEye server environment — the placeholders that need YOUR credentials.
#
# Nothing in this file is set on the VM today. Every feature below is built and
# tested against the seam; each one activates the moment its variables appear,
# with no code change. integrations.py reports which are missing and NEVER
# returns a secret value, so /integrations is safe to look at while signed in.
#
# Copy to /opt/quanthunt/.env on the VM (the deploy excludes .env from rsync,
# so it survives every push) and restart: sudo systemctl restart quanthunt

# ── Sessions ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set this and the cookie key stops depending on a file on one machine.
# Any long random string; changing it signs everyone out exactly once.
# AUTH_SECRET=

# ── Member accounts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# URGENT. The three default passwords are committed to a PUBLIC repository, so
# they are public knowledge and must be ROTATED, not merely hashed.
#
# The easy way, with no SSH to this machine at all:
#   1. python3 deploy/rotate-logins.py     (on your own machine)
#   2. paste what it prints into the GitHub repo secret MEMBER_ACCOUNTS_JSON
#   3. run the Deploy workflow
# The deploy writes /opt/quanthunt/members.json and restarts the service; the
# rsync excludes that file, so later deploys leave it alone.
#
# By hand instead: write the same JSON to /opt/quanthunt/members.json (chmod
# 600), or set the variable below. Either replaces the placeholders entirely.
# One hash at a time:  python -m members hash
# MEMBER_ACCOUNTS_JSON={"you":{"password":"scrypt$...","plan":"pro","name":"You","owner":true}}
# MEMBER_ACCOUNTS_FILE=/opt/quanthunt/members.json

# ── Self-service sign-up ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Open by default. New accounts are never owners and land on MEMBER_SIGNUP_PLAN.
# MEMBER_SIGNUP=closed
# MEMBER_SIGNUP_CODE=some-shared-invite-code
# MEMBER_SIGNUP_PLAN=free

# ── Google sign-in ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# console.cloud.google.com → APIs & Services → Credentials → OAuth client ID
# (Web application). Authorised redirect URI:
#   https://taureye.com/auth/oauth/google/callback
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ── Payments (Razorpay) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# dashboard.razorpay.com → Settings → API Keys. Needs a registered entity, PAN,
# GSTIN and a bank account before Razorpay will approve the account, which is
# the long pole on the launch plan.
# The webhook secret is separate from the API secret: set a webhook pointing at
#   https://taureye.com/billing/webhook
# and paste ITS secret here — verification uses the raw request body.
# RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
# RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
# RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# ── Email (password reset, verification, receipts) ──────────────────────────
# SMTP_HOST=
# SMTP_USER=
# SMTP_PASS=
# SMTP_FROM=TaurEye <no-reply@taureye.com>

# ── Optional tuning ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Credit prices, if the defaults in rewards.py need changing.
# PRICE_DOSSIER=25
# PRICE_BACKTEST=10
# PRICE_DEEP_SCAN=15
# PRICE_AI_EXPLAIN=5
# PRICE_EXPORT=10
# PRICE_EXTRA_ALERT=5
# DAILY_BONUS_CREDITS=5
# REFERRAL_REFERRER_CREDITS=100
# REFERRAL_REFEREE_CREDITS=50

# NSE holidays, so a streak is not broken by a day the market was shut.
# Comma-separated ISO dates.
# NSE_HOLIDAYS=2026-10-02,2026-11-04
